nt.\r\n#   3. NOTHING about the crew switch. `AOA_DISTRIBUTED_CREW_ROLLOUT_ENABLED` is deployment-wide\r\n#      with no per-Organization dimension, so arming it would arm crew for every enabled tenant at\r\n#      once. The base file does not set it and neither does this one; the live profile asserts it\r\n#      is unset or false on every replica (M1 plan §6, S0-8).\r\n#\r\n# ── DEP-019: the journey is WORKER-DRIVEN, and that is four more changes ──────\r\n#\r\n#   4. THE ONE DEPLOYED WORKER DISPATCHES. `worker-b` enters the networked container boot root\r\n#      (`/worker-net-app/dist/bin/networked-host.js`, DEP-011 Slice 2b-ii), with\r\n#      `AOA_WORKER_DISPATCH_ENABLED=1`, a durable event outbox and the DEP-017 env probe armed.\r\n#      ★ SCOPED TO THIS FILE, exactly as DEP-015 scoped `checkDispatchDefaultOff` to its own\r\n#      overlay. `docker-compose.d1.yml` and `scripts/d1-dispatch-expectation.json` are UNCHANGED,\r\n#      so `check-d1-dispatch-declared` still holds BOTH base workers to ABSENT and still reds if\r\n#      anyone sets the flag there. That guard parses only the base file, so the override\'s posture\r\n#      would otherwise be covered by nothing — `evaluateSpineOverrideText` holds it instead, in\r\n#      both directions.\r\n#   5. ITS TARGET IS TENANT A\'S. `worker-b` presents a committed, organization-scoped profile bound\r\n#      to the first enabled spine Organization, and `migrate` seeds THAT profile\'s target and\r\n#      authorizes THAT ticket — one artifact read twice, the WRK-017 shape, with the spine\'s own\r\n#      pair of files. The worker gets its OWN state volume so a device identity minted on the\r\n#      two-worker train can never be presented here.\r\n#      ★ ONE deployed worker means ONE worker-driven tenant. Tenant B\'s journey stays\r\n#      harness-driven and every one of its F10 properties is still asserted; the deployed worker\r\n#      being offered NO work for B or for the control tenant is itself a cross-tenant case, with\r\n#      A\'s own offer as its positive control. Recorded in DEP-019-result.md.\r\n#   6. THE REFERENCE PROVIDER SERVES THE GATED WIRE. `fake-provider` opens a third port speaking\r\n#      the adapter-manager\'s `POST /op/<op>`, over the fake\'s per-op `SandboxProvider`. The\r\n#      shipped `bin/adapter-manager.ts` is untouched and stays `e2b`-only.\r\n#   7. THE CONTROL PLANE MINTS THE RUN CAPABILITY. Without\r\n#      `AOA_CONTROL_PLANE_SIGNING_KEY_FILE` the mint is inert, no `ownedLabelsCapability` rides the\r\n#      secret-resolve reply, and every networked run terminates `no_run_capability` before create.\r\n#      ★ THE KEYPAIR IS GENERATED BY THE JOB, NEVER COMMITTED. `docker/d1/runtime-keys/` is\r\n#      git-ignored and created per run; neither half is printed, and a missing or non-ed25519 key\r\n#      is a refusal to boot on both sides — never an ungated provider wire.\r\n#      ★ THE KEY BOUNDARY, now held by a check. The private half is bound as an individual FILE into\r\n#      the control plane ONLY, and the PUBLIC half as an individual FILE into the reference provider\r\n#      ONLY; `evaluateSpineOverrideText` reds on a DIRECTORY mount of `runtime-keys` into any\r\n#      service. History, because this record must not read as though it was always so: until\r\n#      2026-09-23 both services mounted the whole directory, so the provider — the container that\r\n#      also hosts the child-process probe path — did receive the private capability-minting key,\r\n#      while this block claimed it received only the public half. Codex raised it (P1, PR #572); the\r\n#      false claim was corrected first and the binds were fixed under the planning session\'s ruling.\r\n#      ★ The evidence bundle is NOT scanned for these two values before upload — stated because this\r\n#      block previously claimed it was. `collect-d1-evidence` gathers container logs, job events and\r\n#      a SCHEMA-ONLY `pg_dump`, so neither value is captured today, but that is a property of what\r\n#      the services happen to log rather than a control. Tracked in `DEP-019-result.md` §13.5.\r\n#\r\n# ONE-LINE JSON, single-quoted, on purpose: the static check compares it byte-for-byte.\r\n# =============================================================================\r\n\r\nservices:\r\n  migrate:\r\n    # DEP-019 — seed the SPINE worker\'s target and authorize the SPINE ticket. The base file\'s\r\n    # pair belongs to the two-worker train; the mount source here must equal the one `worker-b`\r\n    # presents below, or the seed authorizes a code nothing presents.\r\n    environment:\r\n      AOA_D1_SEED_WORKER_PROFILE_FILE: "/seed-worker.profile.json"\r\n      AOA_D1_SEED_ENROLMENT_TICKET_FILE: "/seed-enrolment-ticket"\r\n    volumes:\r\n      - "./docker/d1/m1-spine-worker.profile.json:/seed-worker.profile.json:ro"\r\n      - "./docker/d1/m1-spine-worker.enrollment-ticket:/seed-enrolment-ticket:ro"\r\n\r\n  control-plane:\r\n    environment:\r\n      AOA_DISTRIBUTED_EXECUTION_ROLLOUT: \'{"organizations":{"0d016a00-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a":{"mode":"canary","workloads":["batch"]},"0d016b00-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b":{"mode":"canary","workloads":["batch"]}}}\'\r\n      # DEP-019 — the OwnedLabelsCapability mint. Generated per run into a git-ignored directory.\r\n      AOA_CONTROL_PLANE_SIGNING_KEY_FILE: "/keys/control-plane-signing-key.pem"\r\n      # DEP-019 — the secrets master key, GENERATED PER RUN and required (`:?`), never committed\r\n      # and never defaulted. The journey\'s job carries one `env` / `sandbox_local_only` secret\r\n      # handle, because the OwnedLabelsCapability only rides a RESOLVED handle\'s reply; resolving\r\n      # it needs the Company secret store, and the store\'s key must be the same one the seed and\r\n      # the server use. Without `:?` a missing value would silently mint a fresh key inside the\r\n      # container and the seeded secret would decrypt nowhere.\r\n      AOA_SECRETS_MASTER_KEY: "${AOA_D1_SPINE_SECRETS_MASTER_KEY:?the lane generates the per-run secrets master key}"\r\n    volumes:\r\n      # The PRIVATE half, and ONLY here. An individual FILE bind, never the directory (Codex P1).\r\n      - "./docker/d1/runtime-keys/control-plane-signing-key.pem:/keys/control-plane-signing-key.pem:ro"\r\n\r\n  control-plane-b:\r\n    profiles: ["m1-spine-excluded"]\r\n    environment:\r\n      AOA_DISTRIBUTED_EXECUTION_ROLLOUT: \'{"organizations":{"0d016a00-0000-4000-8000-00000000000a":{"mode":"canary","workloads":["batch"]},"0d016b00-0000-4000-8000-00000000000b":{"mode":"canary","workloads":["batch"]}}}\'\r\n\r\n  worker-a:\r\n    profiles: ["m1-spine-excluded"]\r\n\r\n  fake-provider:\r\n    environment:\r\n      # DEP-019 — the GATED provider wire. Arming the port without the PUBLIC key is a refusal to\r\n      # boot (fake-provider-entry.mjs), because `createProviderServer` leaves create + execute on\r\n      # raw, ungated handlers when its key is undefined.\r\n      AOA_FAKE_PROVIDER_WIRE_PORT: "8082"\r\n      AOA_FAKE_PROVIDER_CONTROL_PLANE_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE: "/keys/control-plane-public-key.pem"\r\n    volumes:\r\n      - "./tests/fixtures/distributed-execution:/fixtures:ro"\r\n      # The PUBLIC half, and ONLY the public half. An individual FILE bind: mounting the DIRECTORY\r\n      # handed this container the private capability-minting key as well, which matters more than\r\n      # usual because this is also the container that hosts the child-process probe execution path\r\n      # (Codex P1, PR #572). `evaluateSpineOverrideText` now reds on a directory mount of\r\n      # `runtime-keys` into any service, so the boundary is held by a check and not by this comment.\r\n      - "./docker/d1/runtime-keys/control-plane-public-key.pem:/keys/control-plane-public-key.pem:ro"\r\n\r\n  worker-b:\r\n    # DEP-019 — the NETWORKED container boot root. The base image CMD (`worker-daemon.js`) injects\r\n    # no provider and is inert `no_provider`; the base compose\'s `container-host.js` override is\r\n    # the custody path without one. This bin wraps that same custody path and adds the per-run\r\n    # `makeRunProvider` factory over `AOA_WORKER_PROVIDER_URL`.\r\n    command: ["node", "/worker-net-app/dist/bin/networked-host.js"]\r\n    environ'... 1815 more characters,
